  "description": "Every context hypothesis in the tail was discharged by ONE letter: no other term shared the source's first letter, so 'no other term extends this context' followed from List.cons.inj regardless of which context the lemma picked. This measures that sufficient condition step by step across the prefix, alongside the longest common prefix with any other entry -- which says how much work a failing step needs, a clash at length 1 being a different problem from one at length 9. The necessary condition (no duplicated redex word) was already measured clean chain-wide by hecke-prefix-schedule-check.",
  "parameters": {
    "head_separation": "no other list entry shares the source word's first letter",
    "why_it_matters": "where it holds, the step needs no collision reasoning at all, for any lemma and any choice of left context",
    "head_clashing_steps": "4(a-1), independent of b",
    "steps_with_NO_satisfiable_left_context": "2a, independent of b",
    "but_the_precise_condition_holds_at_all_of_them": "hpark is SUFFICIENT, not necessary. What a step needs is that its SOURCE be absent from the rest of the list (monicStep's hne), and a bundled lemma needs that at each of its own intermediate sources -- which is exactly the relaxation farComm_transport_right_sources already carries, excluding only the split naming the final word. Measured: every source in the chain is unique, the 2a hard-core steps included. So the 2a figure measures a LEMMA-SHAPE problem (blockTransportRight / blockPassFromTwo / blockPass / loopTwoGen do not propagate the relaxation), not a mathematical obstruction.",
    "phase_split": "the clashes are a CONTIGUOUS SUFFIX beginning at step a^2-3a+9: the prefix opens with a^2-3a+9 steps that are entirely head-separated and therefore need no collision reasoning at all, and closes with 4(a-1) steps where the two lineages have converged enough to share prefixes",
    "hpark_criterion": "a left context A is necessarily a PREFIX of the source (the lemmas read the source as A ++ redex ++ tail), so hpark -- no other term r is A ++ z -- holds exactly when lcp(source, r) < |A| for every r. |A| reaches at most the redex offset kk, so a working context exists iff kk > max_r lcp. This is the ACTUAL criterion; head separation is only a proxy for it, and overstates the difficulty by 2(a-2).",
    "head_separated_steps": "a^2 - 3a + 9",
    "deepest_shared_prefix": "2a + 1, independent of b",
    "reordering": "both lineage-grouped schedules are measured too, since scheduling is exactly what repaired the tail's clash; both are legal and reach the same endpoint, and NEITHER reduces the clash count"
  },
