  "caveats": [
    "Head separation is SUFFICIENT, not necessary -- see the sharper kk > lcp criterion, which is what actually decides satisfiability.",
    "`context_fits` is OPTIMISTIC: it says a working left context EXISTS at the full redex offset. A given lemma may force a shorter A (e.g. blockPass's A stops where the block begins), in which case that step is harder than this column suggests. The 2a `context_does_not_fit` figure is the robust one -- there NO length works.",
    "Only three schedules are measured -- the engine's and the two lineage-groupings. The space of legal orders is far larger, so a clash surviving all three is not proved unavoidable."
  ]
